Hi,

You can use specific bootstrap classes that will render your application differently depending on the device used. See the Shiny layout guide <https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/wiki/Shiny-Application-Layout-Guide> for some suggestions on this.

Alternatively, you can use jQuery to obtain height and width information and use this to set specific width variables. In jQuery these are available via $(window).width() etc, see here <https://api.jquery.com/width/>. Then instead of expressing variables in a fixed number of pixels, you express them as a function of the width info obtained via jQuery. This would require you to add some javascript to your code, which may unnecessarily complicate your code.

An advantage of the bootstrap classes is that they automatically do the computations for you, however, you may have less control over what you want to do precisely.

caveat: I'm definitely not an expert in HTML5/CSS, so take my suggestions with a pinch of salt please ;-)

