I managed to solve it. The idea was to convert data.frame to a list of the lists so I can refer to event in the tooltip similar to Example 11 in here:
https://github.com/ramnathv/rCharts/blob/master/inst/libraries/highcharts/examples.R

##############
data <- data.frame(x = seq(1:10), y = runif(10), event = c(rep(NA,4), "event1", "event2", rep(NA,4)))

p <- Highcharts$new()
p$xAxis(categories = unique(factor(data[, 'x'])), labels=list(rotation=-90, y=40))
p$yAxis(min=0)
p$legend(align = "right", verticalAlign = "right", layout = "vertical")

p$series(data=data[,'y'],
         type='line',
         name="series 1"
)

data_events <- data
data_events[,'events_y'] <- data_events[,'y']
data_events[,'events_y'][is.na <http://is.na>(data_events[,'event'])] <- NA
data_events <- apply(data_events[,c('events_y','event')], 1, function(x) list(y=as.numeric(x[1]), event=as.character(x[2])))

p$series(data=data_events,

         type='scatter',
         linkedTo=':previous',
         marker = list(symbol = 'url(http://www.highcharts.com/demo/gfx/sun.png)')
)

p$tooltip(formatter = "#! function() { return this.series.name <http://this.series.name> + '<br>' + (typeof this.point.event != 'undefined' ? this.point.event : ' ') ; } !#")
p
###########

The key is this line: data_events <- apply(data_events[,c('events_y','event')], 1, function(x) list(y=as.numeric(x[1]), event=as.character(x[2])))

If any of you have any suggestions how to improve the code or different and more efficient approach please let me know!

Thank you.

K

