> I have made some modifications to your code - the logic of it all is totally screwed up (don't wanna waste my time debugging that) but it manages to update at intervals:
>
> library(shiny)
>
> ui <- basicPage(
>     tags$p(actionButton("increment", "+1")),
>     tags$p(actionButton("decrement", "-1")),
>     tags$p(actionButton("step", "Step count")),
>     uiOutput("count"),
>     textOutput("result")
> )
>
> max_steps <- 40
> step_size <- 3
>
> server <- function(input, output, session) {
>     values <- reactiveValues(i = 1, isCounting = FALSE, endCount = NULL, nextBreak = NULL)
>
>     output$count <- renderText({
>         paste0("i = ", values$i)
>     })
>
>     observe({
>         input$increment
>         values$i <- isolate({values$i}) + 1
>     })
>
>     observe({
>         input$decrement
>         values$i <- isolate({values$i}) - 1
>     })
>
>     # Start counting on observing input$step
>     observe({
>         input$step
>
>         isolate({
>             values$isCounting <- TRUE
>             values$endCount <- values$i + max_steps
>         })
>     })
>     observe({
>         if(values$isCounting) {
>             isolate({
>                 values$nextBreak <- values$i+step_size
>             })
>             invalidateLater(1, session)
>         }
>     })
>
>     # Counter code that will be invoked when isCounting is first set and then reinvoked
>     # until the endCount has been reached.
>     counter <- reactive({
>         cat("In counter(), i = ", values$i, "\n")
>
>         isolate({
>             if(!values$isCounting) return("Not counting")
>
>             if(!values$isCounting && values$i >= values$endCount) {
>                 values$isCounting <- FALSE
>                 return("Not counting")
>             }
>         })
>         num_steps <- min(values$nextBreak - values$i, isolate(values$endCount - values$i))
>
>         ### Perform real and possible long-running calculation here:
>         Sys.sleep(1)
>         ans <- paste("steps = ", num_steps)
>         ###
>
>         isolate(values$i <- values$i + num_steps)
>         return(ans)
>     })
>
>     output$result <- reactive({counter()})
> }
>
> runApp(list(ui = ui, server = server))
>
> The gist of it all is to have the invalidateLater() call within an observer (didn't realise this when I posted the previous answer). That observer is responsible for determining whether the loop should continue or not, as well as setting some reactive values needed for the main function to perform the next batch of the calculation. It feels a bit convoluted, I'll give you that, but it gets the job done. This is something I'll probably use a lot so hopefully I'll converge onto a simplistic standard setup for this... Let me know if you get it to work
