Do not use class(x) == 'try-error'. Use inherits(x, 'try-error'),
because class(x) might be a vector of length greater than one.

With the next version of shiny (0.10; currently on Github
https://github.com/yihui/shiny), you will be able to define such
custom error messages via validate(), e.g.

# in server.R
function(input, output, session) {
  renderPlot({
    validate(need(Proc()$WEIGHT, "Data not available!"))
  })
}

Regards,
Yihui

